SUMMARY:Valley Forge Park River Trail (Pawlings Rd)
DESCRIPTION:Walking Tails\nDirections: From the intersection of Egypt Road
  and Park Ave./Pawlings Road\, proceed on Pawlings Road heading towards th
 e Schuylkill River. You will pass Mill Grove on your right\, St. Gabriel H
 all on your left and Pawling Farm on your left. You are getting close when
  you pass Sullivan Blvd. on your left and Gertrude St. on your right. You 
 turn left on the next and last left (right before you go over the bridge o
 ver the Schuylkill River). Look for the River Trail Valley Forge Park sign
  visible from Pawlings Road. The gravel parking lot is straight ahead and 
 also visible from Pawlings Road. If you go over the bridge over the Schuyl
 kill River\, you have gone too far and are now in Chester county.\n\nCLICK
  DIRECTLY ON THE MAP IF YOU THINK YOU ARE LOST. IT WILL BRING YOU RIGHT TO
  US WHERE WE MEET.\n\nThis walk goes out about 1.5 miles along the Schuylk
 ill River and then we come back the way we came\, for a total of 3 miles. 
 This is a dirt/gravel/mulch trail through the woods.\n\nStart Time: Arrive
  a few minutes early. We will start hiking promptly at the scheduled time.
 \n\nDuration of the walk – depends on the people and dogs in the group. 
 We frequently end up walking in smaller packs based on the comfort level o
 f the participants.\n\nIn the past this walk takes a little over an hour.\
 n\nPlease remember pooh bags and that your dog must be on a leash that is 
 no more than 10 feet long. Sturdy shoes or hiking boots are recommended. D
 ress appropriately for weather conditions.\n\nNOTICE: By attending this ev
 ent you are agreeing that YOU ARE RESPONSIBLE FOR YOUR OWN SAFETY AT ALL T
 IMES. The hike leader and other members cannot be held responsible for any
  damages\, accidents\, or liabilities incurred while hiking with us.\n\nVa
 lley Forge Trail Map ([http://www.nps.gov/vafo/planyourvisit/maps.htm](htt
 p://www.nps.gov/vafo/planyourvisit/maps.htm))
